Week 3 Report — Daily and Sports Activities Dataset

What I did this week

This week I built two deep learning models: a 1D CNN and a Bidirectional LSTM. Both models read the raw sensor signal directly. This is different from the Random Forest in week 2 which only used statistics like mean and standard deviation.

1D CNN model

I built a CNN with 3 convolutional blocks. Each block has Conv1d, BatchNorm, ReLU, and MaxPool layers. After the blocks there is a global average pooling and two fully connected layers. The input shape is (N, 45, 125) because Conv1d needs channels first. I trained it with Adam optimizer, learning rate 0.001, and early stopping with patience 10.

BiLSTM model

I built a Bidirectional LSTM with 2 layers and hidden size 128. Because it is bidirectional the output size is 256. I added LayerNorm, Dropout, and two fully connected layers. I used gradient clipping with max norm 1.0 to stop exploding gradients during training. Scheduler was ReduceLROnPlateau.

